{"agent_id":"pp3g-5jfH-re-review-the-revised-154-durable-opencode-silent-205b","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-05T23:08:31.480800247Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"235a3a4a-bbad-43e5-8623-c3eed7023bf4","comment_uuid":"765e03e8-9896-4c42-871b-daaf818993a1","author":"pp3g-5jfH-re-review-the-revised-154-durable-opencode-silent-205b","content":"# RE-REVIEW VERDICT r2 — #154 durable silent-hang fix design (REVISED #180)\n\n**Verdict: PASS**\n\nThe revised design on #180 closes every round-1 blocker and finding (B1-B3, F4-F13, R1-R3) with sufficient specificity for implementation. I re-derived each checkable claim against the design source independently — the change-log is accurate.\n\n---\n\n## Findings-by-finding verification\n\n### B1 — BOTH guard copies patched: PASS\n\n§2.1 provides reachability evidence for the v2 aiskd.ts copy: (a) harness logs contain v1-only lines (message=process, message=\"llm runtime selected\"); (b) #144 four ProviderHeaderTimeoutError entries can only come from v1 (v2 has no headerTimeout); (c) v2 SessionRunner uses LLMClient routes that do not touch aiskd.ts; (d) no configured provider registers through v2 AISDK hooks. The conclusion — patch both as defense-in-depth with parity to the #145 interim — is sound. §6.5 codifies a rebase re-check (grep-count content-type guard = 0 in both files). The error-class note (v2 plain Error vs v1 APIError) is documented as a v2-path limitation, not a gap.\n\n### B2 — Option A' idle-progress deadline adopted: PASS\n\n§3.1 adopts bodyIdleTimeout=600_000 (10 min, resets per chunk) with opt-in bodyAbsoluteTimeout=3_300_000 (55 min) default OFF. §3.2 trade-off table shows A' dominates A (no false-abort on slow-but-progressing) and B (no false-abort on long streaming non-SSE). §3.3 numeric chain: bodyIdleTimeout x max POSTs = 600_000 x 3 = 1_800_000 ms (30 min) < request timeout (3_600_000 = 60 min) < operator timeout. §3.4 documents Option B false-abort class (Bedrock eventstream, ndjson, text/plain streaming) — the correct reason B was rejected. §3.5 acknowledges the acceptable trade-off (body pausing > 10 min between chunks).\n\n### B3 — Error-class-scoped retry budget + off-by-one fixed: PASS\n\n§4.2 replaces blanket RETRY_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3 with RETRY_MAX_RETRIES=2. meta.attempt is 1-based retry count (verified by designer against retry.ts:65 — delay(1)=2000ms). Stop at meta.attempt > 2 => initial + 2 retries = exactly 3 POSTs. Bounded class: ProviderResponseStreamError, ProviderHeaderTimeoutError, ECONNRESET. Unbounded class: 429/usage-limit with retry-after preserved (verified upstream test waits >10min). §4.2 item 2 documents the deliberate no-elapsed-budget decision for rate-limit class. §4.2 item 4 pins second retry layer (input.retries = 0). §4.2 item 5 notes distinct error messages share class code. §3.3 verifies per-attempt ceiling: each POST bounded by first of {bodyIdleTimeout, bodyAbsoluteTimeout, request timeout}.\n\n### F4 — Per-attempt WARN + grep-asserted ERROR: PASS\n\n§4.2 item 1 adds Effect.logWarning(\"retry\", {provider, attempt, code, nextDelay}) in SessionRetry.policy() step, plus terminal Effect.logWarning(\"retry budget exhausted\", {attempt, code, total POSTs: meta.attempt+1}). §7 test 13 grep-asserts >= 1 level=ERROR line + per-attempt level=WARN message=\"retry\" + terminal budget-exhausted WARN. The acceptance criterion is grep-asserted, not eyeballed.\n\n### F5 — Turn-level parsed-stream guard + instrumentation + real-provider capture: PASS\n\n§5.1 identifies the causal gap: production timeout: 3600000 is request-level AbortSignal.timeout that fires on raw body stall (#145 proved at 15s) but cannot produce the 10.9h zero-retry zero-error signature (#142/OZWZ) — the stall is above the raw-body layer (llm.ts:373 fullStream with no deadline). §5.2 item 2 adds Stream.timeoutFail({duration: Duration.millis(llmIdleTimeout), error: () => new ResponseStreamError(\"Turn stalled...\")}) — resets per parsed event, opt-in config, throws ResponseStreamError flowing into bounded retry budget (§4). §5.2 item 1 adds content-type/transport logging at stream start and per-parsed-event progress at DEBUG. §7 test 9b covers parsed-stream stall. §7 test 15 captures real-provider content-type/transport/stall-layer.\n\n### F6-F7 — wrapBodyIdle pull() shape + lifecycle: PASS\n\n§2.2 Patch A Hunk 1 shows the full wrapBodyIdle implementation: ReadableStream with async pull(ctrl) — one read per pull, timer inside the Promise, settled guard prevents ctrl.close() after ctrl.error(), clearTimeout runs on done and in cancel(), cancel promise gets .catch(() => {}). §2.2 lifecycle notes explicitly call out each hardened point. The absolute-cap timer is cleared on done/cancel. §7.3 test 5 verifies idle fires on gap > ms, slow progress does not fire, done/cancel clear timers, absolute cap fires only when configured.\n\n### F8 — Opt-in bodyIdleTimeout: PASS\n\n§2.2 Patch A Hunk 2: bodyIdleTimeout extracted from options and deleted (mirrors chunkTimeout/headerTimeout pattern). wrapBodyIdle is opt-in: if (typeof ms !== \"number\" || ms <= 0) return res. Dispatcher routes SSE -> wrapSSE, non-SSE -> wrapBodyIdle, unconfigured -> unwrapped. Absent content-type -> non-SSE branch (§7.4 checks absent content-type). §7 test 10 covers gzip (compressed bodies safe under wrapper). §7 test 11 covers non-chat requests (unconfigured -> unwrapped; configured -> completes correctly).\n\n### F9 — POST-count invariant + second retry layer pinned: PASS\n\n§4.2 item 3: RETRY_MAX_RETRIES=2 with meta.attempt > 2 => <= 3 POSTs, asserted in POST counts (server-side counter), not attempt indices. §4.2 item 4: input.retries pinned to 0, assert unset. §7 test 14: server-side counter <= 3 for hang scenarios.\n\n### F10 — Atomic mv: PASS\n\n§6.2: stage to .opencode.exe.new, chmod +x, then mv to live target (same-fs atomic rename). Backup rotation: previous fork binary moved to backup before new one installed. §6.3 rollback uses the same atomic swap pattern.\n\n### F11 — Workspace-root bun install + pin: PASS\n\n§6.1: bun pinned to v1.3.14 (from repo packageManager field). bun install at workspace root (not inside packages/opencode) so root postinstall (fix-node-pty) runs. --skip-embed-web-ui decision documented (accepted if app build fails; TUI unaffected). Build prereqs explicitly listed.\n\n### F12 — Fork-identity marker + drift detection: PASS\n\n§6.4: OPENCODE_VERSION=1.18.13-pp3g-fork OPENCODE_CHANNEL=fork-pp3g at build time (from build.ts:192-199); opencode --version reports fork marker. Launch-time drift detection: wrapper asserts fork marker before exec, prints error and exit 1 on mismatch. Watcher drift check added for non-wrapper launches. Runtime string marker (\"Body read timed out\") greppable for presence checks.\n\n### F13 — Interim stopgap status: PASS\n\n§6.0 Step 0: documents autoupdate: false already set and #179 byte patch already applied (both copies). Implementation step 0 is re-verify stopgap before/during fork build; re-apply #145 procedure if wipe detected.\n\n### R2 — Test-6 gaps > chunkTimeout: PASS\n\n§7.1 test 6: SLOW_CHUNK_MS=5000, 5 chunks, chunkTimeout=3000, bodyIdleTimeout=30000. Gaps (5s) exceed chunkTimeout (3s) — discriminates A' from A (gap > chunkTimeout => Option A would false-abort). Test 6b adds never-completes variant (aborts at bodyIdleTimeout).\n\n### R3 — PER_REQUEST mode: PASS\n\n§7.1 test 7: PER_REQUEST server mode — request #1 hangs, request #2 healthy. Source-confirmed downgrade documented: provider.ts:1746 constructs new AbortController() inside the per-call fetch closure (only SDK instance memoised). §7.4 consumer cancellation test covers cancel path.\n\n### Verification matrix sufficiency: PASS\n\nMatrix expanded from 8 tests (#175) to 15 tests + 3 additional checks (§7.4). Coverage includes: stalled-but-not-dead (test 9), parsed-stream stall (test 9b), gzip (test 10), non-chat (test 11), fork unit tests (test 12), grep-assert ERROR (test 13), POST counts (test 14), real-provider capture (test 15), wrapper survival + consumer cancellation + exit-code verification (§7.4).\n\n---\n\n## Minor observations (non-blocking)\n\n1. Wrapper survival test (#177 finding 3): the drift detection mechanism (§6.4) and §7.4 wrapper survival check conceptually cover this, but the exact test procedure (simulate npm upgrade, assert wrapper resolves fork binary) is documented as a §7.4 additional check rather than in the main matrix table. The implementer should ensure this is a runnable assertion, not just a described check.\n\n2. Consumer cancellation test (#177 finding 5): similarly, §7.4 describes it but the wrapBodyIdle cancel() implementation (§2.2) already handles this path correctly with settled guard + clearTimeout + reader.cancel. The test just needs to exercise it.\n\n3. Exit-code verification (#177 finding / r3 N4): §7.4 lists it as an additional check. The implementer should assert opencode run returns non-zero on session error, not just assume it.\n\nThese are implementer-time details, not design gaps. The design is implementation-ready.\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n| Finding | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| B1 — both guard copies | PASS | §2.1 reachability evidence, §2.3 patch B, §6.5 rebase re-check |\n| B2 — Option A' idle-progress | PASS | §3.1-3.5, numeric chain, false-abort class documented |\n| B3 — error-class budget + off-by-one | PASS | §4.2, RETRY_MAX_RETRIES=2, meta.attempt > 2, <= 3 POSTs |\n| F4 — per-attempt WARN + grep-assert | PASS | §4.2 item 1, §7 test 13 |\n| F5 — turn-level guard + instrumentation | PASS | §5.1-5.2, llmIdleTimeout, §7 tests 9b/15 |\n| F6-F7 — wrapBodyIdle lifecycle | PASS | §2.2 Hunk 1, settled/clearTimeout/.catch |\n| F8 — opt-in bodyIdleTimeout | PASS | §2.2 Hunk 2, §7 tests 10/11 |\n| F9 — POST-count invariant | PASS | §4.2 items 3-4, §7 test 14 |\n| F10 — atomic mv | PASS | §6.2 stage+mv+backup |\n| F11 — bun install + pin | PASS | §6.1, bun-v1.3.14, workspace-root, postinstall |\n| F12 — fork-identity + drift | PASS | §6.4, OPENCODE_VERSION/CHANNEL, wrapper+watcher assertion |\n| F13 — interim stopgap | PASS | §6.0 Step 0 |\n| R2 — test-6 gaps | PASS | §7.1 test 6, 5s gaps > 3s chunkTimeout |\n| R3 — PER_REQUEST mode | PASS | §7.1 test 7, provider.ts:1746 source-confirmed |\n| Matrix sufficiency | PASS | 15 tests + 3 additional checks, all gaps covered |\n\n**Verdict: PASS — the revised #180 design is implementation-ready.**","created_at":"2026-08-05T23:08:31.470484446Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:5IRL6pj8V7DvhdOhcIcdgkoyzNKPQLMymlbbET//O7k","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgjQd9JWePYj6P6K1vldKplxxadZ3/FK/ytF7RE+O3hk0AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAl6yoKahTOhY0adnR/3OmI8bTEQvOluLYPMjpELTglGwUYj3POTSZpzZTlfXtDvFyXOCcbS0P/0O1ArO3Fj/GDA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:5IRL6pj8V7DvhdOhcIcdgkoyzNKPQLMymlbbET//O7k","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgjQd9JWePYj6P6K1vldKplxxadZ3/FK/ytF7RE+O3hk0AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDhVK/mi2ZNUhmL0b35yhmoU1QAD4afSiiSTuDA+Rph9jNL/kirrAOAqh9VWOE+yniF3EwCulPdEo8GD0yP6UwA="}
